<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans";
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  h1, h2, h3 { font-weight: bold; }
  .header-info { margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .section-header { margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold; }
  .line-item-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 10px; }
  .line-item-table td { padding: 5px 0; }
</style>

<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: center;">
    <!-- Placeholder for Logo -->
    <div style="width: 80px; height: 80px; margin: 0 auto 10px;">[Logo Placeholder]</div>
    <h1 style="font-size: 18pt; margin: 0;">Alabama Agricultural and Mechanical University</h1>
    <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; margin: 5px 0 0;">Office of Human Resources</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="header-info">
    <p>Mailing Address: <span data-field="mailing_address">{{ mailing_address }}</span></p>
    <p>Phone: <span data-field="phone_number">{{ phone_number }}</span></p>
    <p>Fax: <span data-field="fax_number">{{ fax_number }}</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">CERTIFICATION OF HEALTH CARE PROVIDER FOR EMPLOYEE'S SERIOUS HEALTH CONDITION (Family and Medical Leave Act of 1993)</div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p>Section I: For completion by the Employer:</p>
    <p>Employee's job title: <span data-field="employee_job_title">{{ employee_job_title }}</span></p>
    <p>Employee's essential job functions: <span data-field="employee_essential_functions">{{ employee_essential_functions }}</span></p>
    <p>Regular work schedule: <span data-field="regular_work_schedule">{{ regular_work_schedule }}</span></p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p>Check if job description is attached: <span data-field="job_description_attached">{{ job_description_attached }}</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header">Section II: For completion by the Employee.</div>
  <p>Please complete Section II before giving this form to your medical provider. The FMLA permits an employer to require that you submit a timely, complete, and sufficient medical certification to support a request for FMLA leave due to your own serious health condition. If requested by your employer, your response is required to obtain or retain the benefit of FMLA protections. Failure to provide a complete and sufficient medical certification may result in a denial of your FMLA request. Your employer must give you at least fifteen (15) calendar days to return this form.</p>
  <p>Employee's name: <span data-field="employee_name">{{ employee_name }}</span></p>
  <p>First: <span data-field="employee_first_name">{{ employee_first_name }}</span></p>
  <p>Middle: <span data-field="employee_middle_name">{{ employee_middle_name }}</span></p>
  <p>Last: <span data-field="employee_last_name">{{ employee_last_name }}</span></p>

  <div class="section-header">Section III: For completion by the Health Care Provider.</div>
  <p>Instructions to the Health Care Provider: Your patient has requested leave under the FMLA. Answer, fully, and completely, all applicable parts. Several questions seek a response as to the frequency or duration of a condition, treatment, etc. Your answer should be your best estimate based upon your medical knowledge, experience, and examination of the patient. Be as specific as you can; terms such as "lifetime," "unknown," or "indeterminate" may not be sufficient to determine FMLA coverage. Limit your responses to the condition for which the employee is seeking leave. Please be sure to sign the form on page 4.</p>
  <p>Provider's name and business address: <span data-field="provider_name">{{ provider_name }}</span></p>
  <p>Type of practice/medical specialty: <span data-field="provider_specialty">{{ provider_specialty }}</span></p>
  <p>Telephone: <span data-field="provider_phone">{{ provider_phone }}</span></p>
  <p>Fax: <span data-field="provider_fax">{{ provider_fax }}</span></p>

  <div style="margin-top: 50px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
    <p>Alabama A&M University</p>
    <p>FMLA Certification of Physician or Practitioner Form</p>
    <p>Office of Human Resources</p>
    <p>July 2016</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-header">Part A: Medical Facts</div>
  <p>Do not provide information about genetic tests, as defined in 29 C.F.R. § 1635.3(f), genetic services, as defined in 29 C.F.R. § 1635.3(e), or the manifestation of disease or disorder in the employee's family members, 29 C.F.R. § 1635.3(b).</p>

  <p>1. Approximate date condition commenced: <span data-field="approximate_start_date">{{ approximate_start_date }}</span></p>
  <p>Probable duration of condition: <span data-field="probable_duration">{{ probable_duration }}</span></p>

  <p>Mark below as applicable:</p>
  <p>Was the patient admitted for an overnight stay in a hospital, hospice, or residential medical care facility? <span data-field="admitted_hospital">{{ admitted_hospital }}</span> No <span data-field="admitted_hospital_yes">{{ admitted_hospital_yes }}</span> Yes. If so, dates of admission: <span data-field="admission_dates">{{ admission_dates }}</span></p>

  <p>Date(s) you treated the patient for condition: <span data-field="treatment_dates">{{ treatment_dates }}</span></p>

  <p>Will the patient need to have treatment visits at least twice per year due to the condition? <span data-field="treatment_twice_yearly">{{ treatment_twice_yearly }}</span> No <span data-field="treatment_twice_yearly_yes">{{ treatment_twice_yearly_yes }}</span> Yes</p>

  <p>Was medication, other than over-the-counter medication, prescribed? <span data-field="medication_prescribed">{{ medication_prescribed }}</span> No <span data-field="medication_prescribed_yes">{{ medication_prescribed_yes }}</span> Yes.</p>

  <p>Was the patient referred to other health care provider(s) for evaluation or treatment (e.g., physical therapist)? <span data-field="referred_provider">{{ referred_provider }}</span> No <span data-field="referred_provider_yes">{{ referred_provider_yes }}</span> Yes. If so, state the nature of such treatments and expected duration of treatment: <span data-field="referred_treatment_details">{{ referred_treatment_details }}</span></p>

  <p>2. Is the medical condition pregnancy? <span data-field="condition_pregnancy">{{ condition_pregnancy }}</span> No <span data-field="condition_pregnancy_yes">{{ condition_pregnancy_yes }}</span> Yes. If so, expected delivery date: <span data-field="expected_delivery_date">{{ expected_delivery_date }}</span></p>

  <p>3. Use the information provided by Alabama A&M University in Section I to answer this question. If Alabama A&M University fails to provide a list of the employee's essential functions or a job description, answer these questions based upon the employee's own description of his/her job functions.</p>
  <p>Can the employee perform any of his/her job functions due to the condition: <span data-field="can_perform_job_functions">{{ can_perform_job_functions }}</span> No <span data-field="can_perform_job_functions_yes">{{ can_perform_job_functions_yes }}</span> Yes.</p>
  <p>If not, identify the job functions the employee is unable to perform: <span data-field="unable_job_functions">{{ unable_job_functions }}</span></p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-header">Part B: Amount of Leave Needed</div>

  <p>5. Will the employee be incapacitated for a single continuous period of time due to his/her medical condition, including any time for treatment and recovery? <span data-field="incapacitated_single_period">{{ incapacitated_single_period }}</span> No <span data-field="incapacitated_single_period_yes">{{ incapacitated_single_period_yes }}</span> Yes</p>

  <p>If so, estimate the beginning and ending dates for the period of incapacity: <span data-field="incapacity_start_date">{{ incapacity_start_date }}</span> to <span data-field="incapacity_end_date">{{ incapacity_end_date }}</span></p>

  <p>6. Will the employee need to attend follow-up treatment appointments or work part-time or on a reduced schedule because of the employee's medical condition? <span data-field="follow_up_treatment">{{ follow_up_treatment }}</span> No <span data-field="follow_up_treatment_yes">{{ follow_up_treatment_yes }}</span> Yes.</p>

  <p>If so, are the treatments or the reduced number of hours of work medically necessary? <span data-field="treatments_necessary">{{ treatments_necessary }}</span> No <span data-field="treatments_necessary_yes">{{ treatments_necessary_yes }}</span> Yes</p>

  <p>Estimate treatment schedule, if any, including the dates of any scheduled appointments and the time required for each appointment, including any recovery period: <span data-field="treatment_schedule_details">{{ treatment_schedule_details }}</span></p>

  <p>Estimate the part-time or reduced work schedule the employee needs, if any: <span data-field="reduced_schedule_details">{{ reduced_schedule_details }}</span> days per week from <span data-field="reduced_schedule_start_date">{{ reduced_schedule_start_date }}</span> through <span data-field="reduced_schedule_end_date">{{ reduced_schedule_end_date }}</span>.</p>

  <p>7. Will the condition cause episodic flare-ups periodically preventing the employee from performing his/her job functions? <span data-field="episodic_flare_ups">{{ episodic_flare_ups }}</span> No <span data-field="episodic_flare_ups_yes">{{ episodic_flare_ups_yes }}</span> Yes.</p>
  <p>Is it medically necessary for the employee to be absent from work during the flare-ups? <span data-field="absent_during_flare_ups">{{ absent_during_flare_ups }}</span> No <span data-field="absent_during_flare_ups_yes">{{ absent_during_flare_ups_yes }}</span> Yes. If so, explain: <span data-field="flare_up_explanation">{{ flare_up_explanation }}</span></p>

  <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
    <p>Based upon the patient's medical history and your knowledge of the medical condition, estimate the frequency of flare-ups and the duration of related incapacity that the patient may have over the next six (6) months (e.g., 1 episode every 3 months lasting 1-2 days):</p>
    <p>Frequency: <span data-field="flare_up_frequency">{{ flare_up_frequency }}</span> times per <span data-field="flare_up_frequency_unit">{{ flare_up_frequency_unit }}</span> week(s) <span data-field="flare_up_frequency_unit2">{{ flare_up_frequency_unit2 }}</span> month(s)</p>
    <p>Duration: <span data-field="flare_up_duration">{{ flare_up_duration }}</span> hours or <span data-field="flare_up_duration_unit">{{ flare_up_duration_unit }}</span> day(s) per episode</p>
    <p>Additional information: Identify question number with your additional answer: <span data-field="additional_info_question_number">{{ additional_info_question_number }}</span></p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 60px;">
    <p>Signature of physician: _________________________ Date: <span data-field="physician_date">{{ physician_date }}</span></p>
    <p>Print name of physician: <span data-field="physician_name">{{ physician_name }}</span></p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 50px; padding: 20px; border: 1px solid #ccc;">
    <p>Return this FMLA Certification of Physician or Practitioner Form in person to</p>
    <p>Cheryl K. Johnson, Assistant Director, Office of Human Resources,</p>
    <p>449 Buchanan Way, Normal, Alabama</p>
    <p>Or mail to:</p>
    <p>Human Resources, Alabama A&M University, Normal, Alabama 35762</p>
    <p>Or fax to: <span data-field="return_fax_number">{{ return_fax_number }}</span></p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 50px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
    <p>Alabama A&M University</p>
    <p>FMLA Certification of Physician or Practitioner Form</p>
    <p>Office of Human Resources</p>
    <p>July 2016</p>
  </div>
</div>